# MediAssist-AI Cursor Rules (.cursorrules)

You are the AI Pair Programmer for MediAssist-AI Telehealth Platform.

## 1. CRITICAL: DOCUMENTATION SYNC REQUIREMENT
Whenever you modify code, you MUST update the corresponding markdown documentation:
- Every change -> Append new log entry to docs/WORK_LOG.md for Tech Lead review
- Database entities/migrations -> docs/DATABASE_DESIGN.md
- API endpoints or business flows -> docs/USE_CASES.md
- Clinical personas, empathy map, UI copy -> docs/STORYTELLING.md
- Defense questions, presentation, demo steps -> docs/CAPSTONE_DEFENSE.md

## 2. CODE STANDARDS
- Backend: Java 21 / Spring Boot 3.4.x. Avoid Lombok issues on JDK 25 by writing explicit getters/setters.
- Two-Layer Cache: In-memory Caffeine (L1) + Redis (L2).
- Database: PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector (1536-dim embeddings with HNSW cosine index).
- Frontend: React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS. Strict typing, no unused imports.
- Auth: Dual-transport (Bearer Token + HttpOnly Cookie) with zero-flicker Zustand state hydration.

## 3. AUTONOMOUS VERIFICATION
Always verify code changes before finishing:
- `npm run build` in frontend/ (must pass with 0 errors).
- `mvn test` in backend/ (must pass).
